In ui.html textGeometry(), replace the two lines `const hl = Number.isFinite(lh) ? Math.max(0, (lh - rects[0].height) / 2) : 0; const y = T - hl;` and `const h = B - T + 2 * hl;` with code that:
1. measures the block's own strut once per font, using an out-of-flow probe,
2. anchors on a first-line rect drawn in that font,
3. lets the half-leading go negative.

```js
const lh = parseFloat(cs.lineHeight);
let hl = 0, anchor = T;
if (Number.isFinite(lh)) {
  const key = cs.fontStyle + '|' + cs.fontWeight + '|' + cs.fontSize + '|' + cs.fontFamily;
  if (!S.gh) S.gh = new Map();          // reset alongside S.deco at walk start
  if (!S.gh.has(key)) {
    const p = S.doc.createElement('span');
    p.textContent = 'x';
    p.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:-9999px;top:0;visibility:hidden;white-space:pre;line-height:normal';
    p.style.fontFamily = cs.fontFamily; p.style.fontSize = cs.fontSize;
    p.style.fontWeight = cs.fontWeight; p.style.fontStyle = cs.fontStyle;
    S.doc.body.appendChild(p);
    const rr = S.doc.createRange(); rr.selectNodeContents(p.firstChild);
    const pr = rr.getClientRects()[0];
    S.gh.set(key, pr ? pr.height : rects[0].height);
    p.remove();
  }
  const gh = S.gh.get(key);                 // content-area height of the block's primary font
  hl = (lh - gh) / 2;                       // may be NEGATIVE (leading-none, line-height:.95, text-5xl..9xl)
  const root = rects.find((r) => Math.abs(r.height - gh) < 1 && r.top < T + lh / 2); // first-line rect in the root font (skips emoji/code/sup fragments)
  anchor = root ? root.top : T;
}
const y = anchor - hl;                      // top of the first line box
const h = B + hl - y;                       // equals lines*lh when lh is uniform
```
Notes:
- The probe is absolutely positioned and appended to body, so it never reflows the content being measured.
- Results are cached per font, so there is at most one forced layout per distinct font.
- With line-height 'normal' (NaN) the behaviour is unchanged.
- No code.js change is needed: Figma recomputes the height from lineHeight and splits leading evenly like CSS.
- Auto Layout padding and spacing come from these boxes, so they become correct automatically. Verified on text-hero: pt 25, spacing 8, h1 h = 3 × 79.8.
- Minimal alternative if the probe is unwanted: delete the Math.max(0, …) clamp. That fixes the common single-font headings but stays wrong when the first fragment uses another font.

